01:12:01.480 --> 01:12:09.340
I actually have had my first drinks in a month,
beginning three or four days ago.

01:12:09.340 --> 01:12:16.380
So in prep for the higher altitude and extensive
hiking and so on, I did not want to compromise

01:12:16.380 --> 01:12:18.940
my sleep getting ready for that.

01:12:18.940 --> 01:12:27.360
I thought it would be a good aesthetic practice/proof
of non-dependence to take a 30-day break from

01:12:27.360 --> 01:12:28.360
alcohol.

01:12:28.360 --> 01:12:32.650
So I took a 30-day break from alcohol, felt
great.

01:12:32.650 --> 01:12:39.220
I know that alcohol, especially once it gets
past two drinks, obliterates sleep.

01:12:39.220 --> 01:12:43.970
So I have experimented with other options.

01:12:43.970 --> 01:12:47.620
Number one is simply not having alcohol, just
having peppermint tea or whatever I might

01:12:47.620 --> 01:12:52.140
want to have for flavor at a dinner, which
is perfectly fine most of the time.

01:12:52.140 --> 01:12:54.550
I'm also looking at other options.

01:12:54.550 --> 01:13:01.790
There are some keto beverages, which are non
ethanol-based alcoholic beverages, if that

01:13:01.790 --> 01:13:03.490
makes any sense.

01:13:03.490 --> 01:13:12.400
Where you can actually get a buzz from, say,
I think it's R Butane dial or (R) 1, 3 butanediol.

01:13:12.400 --> 01:13:24.900
Let me just see what — yeah, so 1, 3 butanediol,
also known as (R) 1, 3 butanediol, is not

01:13:24.900 --> 01:13:34.080
great in my experience for performance at
all, but it can give you a slight buzz.

01:13:34.080 --> 01:13:38.310
And please do not — this is not food consumption
advice.

01:13:38.310 --> 01:13:42.890
1,3 butanediol is used mainly as a solvent
for food flavors.

01:13:42.890 --> 01:13:46.420
So FYI, right?

01:13:46.420 --> 01:13:52.140
So there are a number of brands that sell
(R) butane 1, 3 diol.

01:13:52.140 --> 01:13:54.960
I'm mixing up all of my chemistry here.

01:13:54.960 --> 01:14:02.390
So there are some brands that sell hard keto
drinks, and I have been experimenting with

01:14:02.390 --> 01:14:09.170
those as an alternative to ethanol based drinks,
like a gin tonic or something like that.

01:14:09.170 --> 01:14:16.360
It does seem like the hard keto drinks, if
consumed close to bedtime, will still negatively

01:14:16.360 --> 01:14:17.360
affect sleep.

01:14:17.360 --> 01:14:24.250
So if I consume alcohol, I try to do, whether
it's the hard ketones or ethanol, I try to

01:14:24.250 --> 01:14:26.490
consume it on the early side.

01:14:26.490 --> 01:14:31.520
So if I'm having an early dinner, say 5:30
or 6:00, I want to give my body and my liver

01:14:31.520 --> 01:14:37.640
time to metabolize as much as possible before
I lay down to bed.

01:14:37.640 --> 01:14:39.730
That means I'll go out to dinner.

01:14:39.730 --> 01:14:44.120
If I'm going to have a drink, as I did yesterday
for instance — actually, I had two glasses

01:14:44.120 --> 01:14:54.060
of wine last night and I sat at the bar instead
of at a table so I wouldn't be rushed.

01:14:54.060 --> 01:15:01.670
I had two drinks while writing for about 30
minutes before getting my food.

01:15:01.670 --> 01:15:08.570
Because what I didn't want to do is have one
drink with an appetizer, eat a huge entree,

01:15:08.570 --> 01:15:12.870
and have two or three more drinks just to
feel the buzz.

01:15:12.870 --> 01:15:17.810
Ultimately, all of that lands on my system
and needs to be dealt with.

01:15:17.810 --> 01:15:22.460
So those are a few of the thoughts I have,
but I have dramatically cut back on my alcohol

01:15:22.460 --> 01:15:24.210
content or I have dramatically cut back on
my alcohol consumption, and that might change

01:15:24.210 --> 01:15:25.320
depending on where I go.

01:15:25.320 --> 01:15:29.510
