01:24:27.130 --> 01:24:29.120
That question is this.

01:24:29.120 --> 01:24:34.300
In this list of things, five or six or 10
things, whatever your list of priorities might

01:24:34.300 --> 01:24:43.590
be or to dos, which of these, if done, make
other things or all of these things, either

01:24:43.590 --> 01:24:46.790
irrelevant or easier to do?

01:24:46.790 --> 01:24:48.770
So look at this list of 10 things.

01:24:48.770 --> 01:24:53.910
Which of these, if done, make other items
on this list?

01:24:53.910 --> 01:24:59.870
Hopefully many or all of them, easier to do
or irrelevant.

01:24:59.870 --> 01:25:01.300
That is my sorting function.

01:25:01.300 --> 01:25:02.300
That's it.

01:25:02.300 --> 01:25:07.690
Now, on top of that, let's just say that doesn't
yield the clarity I'm hoping for.

01:25:07.690 --> 01:25:15.001
I could look at that list again and ask myself,
which of these, if done or brought to the

01:25:15.001 --> 01:25:19.852
next milestone, would leave me feeling proudest
at the end of the day?

01:25:19.852 --> 01:25:20.890
I know people who do this with workouts.

01:25:20.890 --> 01:25:24.120
I know CrossFit champions who do this with
certain types of workouts.

01:25:24.120 --> 01:25:29.570
Just asking yourself, which of these, if done
or pushed to the next milestone, would lead

01:25:29.570 --> 01:25:31.120
me feeling proudest at the end of the day?

01:25:31.120 --> 01:25:32.170
That's another one.

01:25:32.170 --> 01:25:36.250
A third would be if you're trying to choose
between, say, major projects.

01:25:36.250 --> 01:25:40.370
So you've got this branching tree and you
have three different professional options.

01:25:40.370 --> 01:25:46.370
Let's just say different projects, different
endeavors, joint ventures, whatever, creative

01:25:46.370 --> 01:25:47.370
projects.

01:25:47.370 --> 01:25:53.310
I'll ask myself, which of these, even if it
